<title>SWEDEN: Indosuez stops being Swedish Riksbank market maker.</title>
<headline>Indosuez stops being Swedish Riksbank market maker.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swedish unit of French commercial bank Credit Agricole Indosuez said on Friday it would cease being a primary dealer of government bonds and Treasury bills for Sweden's central bank, the Riksbank.</p>
<p>&quot;We have been a primary dealer for two years and we can state that it is a tough market if you enter it at a late stage,&quot; Mikael Bernander, local treasury head at Indosuez in Stockholm, told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;It is difficult to get the necessary volume to reach profitability,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The Swedish unit of Indosuez will, however, continue as primary dealer on the currency market.</p>
<p>&quot;We have been active in Sweden on the currency side since the mid-eighties where we are established and have a strong position,&quot; Bernander said.</p>
<p>-- Erik Aronsson, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1010</p>
